  "narrative": "No assessments are due. I register a new set of non-duplicative comparisons that target two remaining scientific gaps: whether the already strong main driver associations are modified by measured transcriptomic states or latent copy-number/assay contexts, and whether the secondary PTEN-loss stronger-dependency association resolves in the lower-aneuploidy core-driver-wildtype low-screen-quality context while the unselected high-aneuploidy screen-quality interaction is directly tested. Direction convention: for positive-direction TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss comparisons, a positive signed estimate means higher raw dependency_composite, i.e. weaker composite dependency; for negative-direction SMARCA4-loss, PTEN-loss, and BRCA2-loss comparisons, a positive signed estimate means lower raw dependency_composite, i.e. stronger composite dependency. For interactions, the estimate is signed to the claimed interaction direction. A positive-direction PTEN-loss interaction is interpreted as attenuation of the negative main PTEN-loss effect if the raw PTEN-loss contrast is less negative in the named subgroup than in its complement; the reverse signed estimate would indicate enhancement or no attenuation. The TP53-loss by median-or-high SLFN11 interaction tests whether a high SLFN11 DNA-damage-response-like state amplifies the TP53-loss weaker-dependency association. The KEAP1-loss by high AXL interaction tests whether a more mesenchymal/receptor-tyrosine-kinase-like state amplifies KEAP1-loss weaker dependency. The SMARCA4-loss by high ASCL2 interaction tests whether a stem-like state amplifies SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency. The PTEN-loss by high MYC and PTEN-loss by high SLFN11 interactions test whether proliferation and DNA-damage-response states modify the smaller PTEN-loss stronger-dependency association. The direct PTEN-loss test in lower-aneuploidy core-driver-wildtype low-screen-quality cells completes the screen-quality/aneuploidy/core-driver context map around the already accepted PTEN-loss effect; the unselected high-aneuploidy screen-quality interaction tests whether elevated aneuploidy changes the direction or magnitude of screen-quality modification. KEAP1-loss by research_signature_c and PTEN-loss by copy_number_8q24 are lower-priority but useful context tests for constructed assay and copy-number modification. BRCA2-loss in core-driver-wildtype cells is included because the very large TP53, KEAP1, and SMARCA4 effects may mask a smaller DNA-repair-loss association. Plausible alternatives for all interaction claims are null, attenuating, opposite, or imprecision-limited subthreshold results. Such results would favor effect heterogeneity, confounding by measured context, assay noise, or causal masking rather than broad generalizable modifiers. All conclusions remain observational within-dataset associations, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration-12 explore attempt 2. Direction convention retained: positive signed estimate for TP53/KEAP1 positive-direction claims means weaker dependency; positive signed estimate for SMARCA4/PTEN/BRCA2 negative-direction claims means stronger dependency. Positive-direction PTEN interactions are attenuation tests of the negative PTEN-loss main effect. Main supported pattern remains TP53/KEAP1 loss associated with weaker dependency and SMARCA4 loss/MSI-high associated with stronger dependency. PTEN loss is a smaller but repeatedly observed stronger-dependency association, with residual context heterogeneity. This attempt avoids parent links to claims lacking displayed evidence after the previous rejection. New proposals: transcriptomic modifiers of TP53 (SLFN11), KEAP1 (AXL), SMARCA4 (ASCL2); PTEN modifiers (MYC, SLFN11, 8q24 copy number, screen-quality interaction in elevated aneuploidy); direct PTEN lower-aneuploidy core-driver-wildtype low-screen-quality stratum; BRCA2-loss in core-driver-wildtype cells. These complement already registered untested PTEN context comparisons H191, H215, H217, and H218. No validation requested at explore. If new PTEN context results are decisive and not already replicated, consider one independent validation later only for a borderline claim where an independent interval could realistically resolve threshold."
